          "type": "text",
          "text": "Good \u2014 the GCD timer correctly uses `stateQueue.sync` to access `_audioEngine` safely.\n\nHere's a summary of the fixes:\n\n### Fix 1: Vibration not working\n**`SharedStorage.swift`**: Changed `vibrationEnabled` default from `false` to `true`. Previously, vibration only got enabled during the onboarding demo or a complex notification setup flow \u2014 most users would never have it turned on. Now it's on by default, and users can turn it off in settings if they want.\n\n### Fix 2: Background detection unreliable\n**`SystemAudioClassifier.swift`** \u2014 Three changes:\n\n1. **`configureBackgroundAudioSession()`** now checks if the audio engine stopped and calls `resumeAudioEngine()` to restart it. Previously it only configured the audio session but never restarted the engine.\n\n2. **Added `DispatchSourceTimer` (GCD timer)** that fires every 15 seconds even in background. The existing `Timer.scheduledTimer` health checks get suspended by iOS when the app is backgrounded, so the engine could stop with no recovery mechanism. The GCD timer checks if the engine is running and restarts it.\n\n3. **Foreground resume is more robust** \u2014 now also checks `SharedStorage.soundDetectionState` in case `isSoundDetectionActive` got cleared during background suspension, ensuring detection recovers when you unlock the phone."
